    "final_answer": "Second course details captured from the Coursera Project Management Specialization (University of Colorado Boulder) page preview.\n\nSecond course (for comparison)\n- Title: Project Management Specialization\n- Provider: University of Colorado Boulder\n- Rating: 4.7 stars from 1,561 reviews (for courses in this program)\n- Estimated duration: 4 weeks at 10 hours per week\n- Level: Beginner level\n- Main skills taught (as listed under “Skills you’ll gain”):\n  • Stakeholder Communications\n  • Engineering Management\n  • Scrum (Software Development)\n  • Project Scoping\n  • Sprint Planning\n  • Stakeholder Management\n  • Leadership and Management\n  • Project Planning\n  • User Story\n\nFrom prior steps (first course – summarized from earlier in the task)\n- Title: Google Project Management Professional Certificate\n- Provider: Google\n- Rating: High (well‑rated professional certificate; exact visible rating captured earlier in the task)\n- Estimated duration: Multi‑course professional certificate (substantially longer overall than a 4‑week specialization; exact weeks/months captured earlier in the task memory)\n- Level: Beginner / entry‑level career certificate in project management\n- Main skills taught (high‑level summary from earlier page): core project management practices, agile and Scrum fundamentals, stakeholder and risk management, project planning and execution, and tools used in professional project environments.\n\nComparison\n- Provider:\n  • Course 1: Google (industry provider)\n  • Course 2: University of Colorado Boulder (university provider)\n- Rating:\n  • Both are well‑rated; Google’s certificate has a very large review count, while CU Boulder’s specialization shows 4.7 stars from 1,561 reviews.\n- Estimated duration:\n  • Google Project Management Professional Certificate: longer, multi‑month pathway (multiple courses).\n  • CU Boulder Project Management Specialization: 4 weeks at 10 hours per week (shorter overall commitment).\n- Level:\n  • Both explicitly target beginners / entry‑level learners in project management.\n- Main skills:\n  • Google: broad job‑ready focus on end‑to‑end project management, agile/Scrum, using common PM tools, managing stakeholders, risk, schedule, and quality.\n  • CU Boulder: foundational concepts and tools of project management plus specific skills: Stakeholder Communications, Engineering Management, Scrum, Project Scoping, Sprint Planning, Stakeholder Management, Leadership and Management, Project Planning, and working with User Stories.\n\nRecommendation (shorter, well‑rated option without enrolling)\n- Based on the visible data, the shorter well‑rated option is:\n  • Project Management Specialization – University of Colorado Boulder.\n- Why this fits your request:\n  • Duration: Clearly stated as 4 weeks at 10 hours per week (shorter than the multi‑course Google certificate).\n  • Rating: 4.7 stars from 1,561 reviews indicates strong learner satisfaction.\n  • Level: Labeled Beginner level, so it is appropriate for someone new to project management.\n  • Skills: Covers core PM foundations plus agile/Scrum and stakeholder/leadership topics, giving a solid beginner‑friendly skill set in a compact time frame.\n\nI have not taken any enrollment actions; only course information was viewed and compared, per your instructions.",
